{
 "_about": "Documented invasive-fish list used for officer alerts. Every entry cites where its listing comes from. The list is a starter set for the fish detected in the chosen real datasets; it is NOT a complete national list and does not replace a regulator's own list.",
 "threat_levels": {
  "CRITICAL": "Species is on the IUCN/ISSG list '100 of the World's Worst Invasive Alien Species'. Alert the officer immediately; confirm in the field within days.",
  "HIGH": "Species has a full IUCN Global Invasive Species Database (GISD) profile documenting harmful invasions. Alert the officer; confirm with a field survey.",
  "WATCH": "The sequence cannot be told apart from a listed invasive species and is NOT confirmed. Shown as a possible detection only; send for review or retake before any action."
 },
 "native_range_note": "native_in lists were checked on 2026-10-10 against the GISD species pages (native range) and FishBase country tables; disagreements were resolved conservatively, i.e. a country is only listed when both agree or the species is clearly native there, because a listed country SUPPRESSES the alert. Cyprinus carpio: Iran left out (GISD lists only alien records; Iranian checklists say native only in the Caspian basin). Clarias batrachus: Sri Lanka left out (GISD: alien); FishBase restricts the true native range to Java, so mainland records may be a look-alike (C. aff. batrachus) - listing those countries avoids false alerts on a native fish.",
 "gisd_note": "GISD = Global Invasive Species Database, IUCN SSC Invasive Species Specialist Group, https://www.iucngisd.org",
